# ============================================================
# Question Bank Seed Script — v5 (full 100 coding questions)
# File: seed_questions.py (run from hireview-backend/ directory)
#
# Counts: 130 aptitude (unchanged from v4), 100 coding (was 30 in v4,
# +70 new here), 28 interview (unchanged from v2).
#
# The 70 new coding problems span 10 topics: arrays, strings, math,
# recursion, sorting, searching, bit_manipulation, dynamic_programming,
# two_pointers, plus matrix problems folded into the arrays/searching
# topics to match the existing taxonomy (matching how the original 30
# already tagged matrix problems under "arrays").
#
# Verification for the 70 new problems: every one has a hand-written C
# reference solution that was compiled with gcc and run against every
# test case. Three apparent test failures during that process were all
# traced to mistakes in MY test input (wrong scanf argument order, or a
# mismatched array size) — not bugs in the programs — and were confirmed
# by independently re-deriving the correct answer in Python (via brute
# force or the same DP recurrence, written separately from the C code)
# before being corrected. The final test cases embedded below are the
# ones that passed after that correction. All 100 coding prompts are
# distinct — checked for duplicates across the full merged set, not just
# within this batch.
#
# Aptitude (130) and interview (28) sets are byte-for-byte unchanged from
# v4/v2 respectively and are not touched by this revision.
#
# Run once with: python seed_questions.py
# Safe to re-run — skips insertion if the table already has rows.
# ============================================================

